    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Keller returns for her three-month review through a qualified tactile interpreter. She has completed 11 of 12 weeks of home physical therapy and does the exercises on the other days as well. She has had no falls. The occupational therapy home visit has not happened yet because of a waiting list; meanwhile her own contractor extended the back-step handrail to the bottom step, and she is using those steps again. She feels steadier on stairs and on uneven ground with her guide. She made a speaking trip last month without difficulty. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>No falls; steadier on stairs</td></tr><tr><td>Exercise</td><td>11 of 12 weeks of physical therapy; home exercises daily</td></tr><tr><td>Home changes</td><td>Back-step handrail extended; occupational therapy visit still waiting</td></tr><tr><td>Activity</td><td>One speaking trip with a sighted guide</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

