    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk, improving (Z91.81)</content>. No falls. Every test has improved since intake (Timed Up and Go 13.5 to 12.0 seconds, chair stand 9 to 11, tandem 6 to 8 seconds), and PROMIS physical function has risen from 41 to 44. [S]<list><item>Finish the last week of physical therapy, then continue the home program daily.</item><item>Occupational therapy home visit: the clinic has asked the service to schedule it this month.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall history</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Timed Up and Go, 30-second chair stand, and four-stage balance test</td><td>After the exercise program</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 12.0 seconds, chair stand 11, tandem stance 8 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PROMIS physical function</td><td>At assessment and at reviews</td><td>Completed today</td><td>44, up from 41</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Strength and balance exercise program</td><td>12 weeks, then ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>11 of 12 weeks completed with good adherence</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Home hazard assessment</td><td>After a fall, within about a month</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not done by three months because of a waiting list, a deviation from the plan. The main hazard was corrected by extending the handrail, and she has had no falls. The clinic has escalated the request</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication review for fall-risk drugs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Still no medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Orthostatic blood pressure</td><td>If symptoms</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic, double-length visit, braille materials</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Interpreter present for the whole visit; after-visit summary given in braille</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>No further falls, and a 30-second chair stand of 12 or more by the six-month review. In progress; target 1959-09-14 [S]</item><item>Home changes complete: handrails on both sides of every step, tactile edge strips, and vibrating smoke and carbon monoxide alarms with a bed shaker. In progress; target 1959-09-14 [S]</item><item>A communication access plan in her chart: a qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic for every visit, double-length appointments, braille after-visit summaries, and a hospital communication passport. Outcome by 1959-03-23: Plan recorded and passport written in braille and print [S]</item><item>Keep traveling to speak, with a travel plan for falls and illness. In progress; target 1959-09-14 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: STEADI (Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths and Injuries): Clinical Resources (2024); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); Zhou SY, et al. Training Medical Students in Deaf, DeafBlind, and Hard-of-Hearing Patient Care Through Interactive Lecture and Simulation. MedEdPORTAL 2025;21:11566 (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Occupational therapy home visit this month. Falls review in three months. Next scheduled visit 1959-09-14: six-month falls prevention and function review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
